.TH SSHX-SERVER 1 "2026-11-17" "sshx-server" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sshx\-server \- server daemon for sshx, a secure web-based, collaborative terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshx\-server
.RB [ \-\-port\ \fIPORT\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-listen\ \fIADDRESS\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-secret\ \fISECRET\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-override\-origin\ \fIURL\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-redis\-url\ \fIURL\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-host\ \fIHOSTNAME\fR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sshx\-server
runs the server side of sshx. It serves the web frontend, terminates
WebSocket connections from sshx clients, and routes encrypted session data
between clients through a globally distributed mesh of server instances.
.PP
Session data is end\-to\-end encrypted by clients; the server only sees
ciphertext along with session metadata. Server instances coordinate with each
other over gRPC and persist session metadata in Redis.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-port\ \fIPORT\fR
Port to listen on (default: 8051).
.TP
.BR \-\-listen\ \fIADDRESS\fR
IP address or network interface to listen on (default: ::1).
.TP
.BR \-\-secret\ \fISECRET\fR
Secret used for signing session tokens (defaults to the
.B SSHX_SECRET
environment variable).
.TP
.BR \-\-override\-origin\ \fIURL\fR
Override the origin URL returned by the Open() RPC.
.TP
.BR \-\-redis\-url\ \fIURL\fR
Redis URL for state management (defaults to the
.B SSHX_REDIS_URL
environment variable).
.TP
.BR \-\-host\ \fIHOSTNAME\fR
Hostname of this server, if running multiple servers.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print version.
.SH FILES
The server binds to
.I ::1:8051
by default and must be able to reach its Redis instance and peer servers over
the network.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a server on all interfaces:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sshx\-server \-\-listen "::"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sshx (1)
.PP
https://sshx.io
